    "Second-order maximum function log S-Au+s^(-1); both small-trace cases and torsion absorption; trace inverse bound plus determinant upper/lower bounds give uniform equivalence, including dimension one.",
    "Higher estimates through the fixed scalar Laplacian, real concave extension of logarithmic determinant and Schauder theory; semilinear nonnegative a case uses Delta(au+F)>=-an+Delta F before derivative bounds.",
    "Continuity path for the smooth normalized equation; exponential comparison, extrema potential bounds and invertibility of L-lambda by zero kernel and Fredholm index zero.",
    "First and second scalar variations integrate at a fixed adjoint measure; Hermitian square nonnegative; affine equality only for constant density direction; strict extremum Lipschitz bounds.",
    "Hopf normalization defect equals logarithm of one plus vertical energy; fiber-average bound coefficient 4; zero defect iff base pullback; background Hessian coefficient 2 and its base-pullback equality case.",
