    "Gauduchon linearization factor n/(n-1), drift but no zeroth-order term; twice/once integration-by-parts adjoint cancellation, surface specialization and constant multiplier at eta=gamma.",
    "Hodge-star scaling v=u/(2 pi), six torsion coefficients by three-index antisymmetrization, excluded gradient indices and their differentiated identities; positive background logdet coercivity and weight comparisons.",
    "Largest-eigenvalue perturbation at multiplicity; covariant/coordinate derivative conversion; exact W-to-Z weighted contractions; third derivatives controlled by missing large-weight indices; positive concavity square.",
    "Both eigenvalue configurations: derivative cancellation with E/K absorption and successive epsilon,D2,D1,delta choices; negative smallest eigenvalue yields a weighted Hessian square and lambda/K bound.",
